    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0357" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg297"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic">November 27,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Submit to French lawyer of first rank on whose impartiality you can rely Waller
                    record inclosed in yours of June 27, and get full written opinion upon questions
                    whether court was lawfully organized and had jurisdiction and whether trial and
                    sentence and all the proceedings <pb facs="0358" n="298" xml:id="pg298"/> were
                    or were not according to law; in other words, whether judgment and sentence were
                    valid upon their face without reference to the other. Supplement with written
                    views upon same questions of law, and forward as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
